'''Michael James Dunleavy''' (born May 5, 1961) is an American politician and educator serving since 2018 as the 12th [[List of governors of Alaska|governor of Alaska]]. A member of the [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican Party]], he served from 2013 to 2018 as a member of the [[Alaska Senate]]. He defeated former U.S. senator [[Mark Begich]] in the [[2018 Alaska gubernatorial election|2018 gubernatorial election]] after incumbent governor [[Bill Walker (American politician)|Bill Walker]] dropped out of the race, and he was reelected in [[2022 Alaska gubernatorial election|2022]].

In 2024, Dunleavy was elected chairman of the [[Interstate Oil and Gas Compact Commission]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Downing |first=Suzanne |date=2024-05-22 |title=Gov. Dunleavy elected chairman of Interstate Oil and Gas Compact Commission |url=https://mustreadalaska.com/gov-dunleavy-elected-chairman-of-interstate-oil-and-gas-compacting-commission/ |access-date=2026-06-24 |website=Must Read Alaska |language=en-US}}</ref>

In 2026, President [[Donald Trump]] appointed Dunleavy to a seat on the [[United States Arctic Research Commission]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ruskin |first=Liz |date=2026-04-16 |title=Trump appoints Alaska governor to a seat on U.S. Arctic Research Commission |url=https://alaskapublic.org/news/2026-04-15/trump-appoints-alaska-governor-to-a-seat-on-u-s-arctic-research-commission |access-date=2026-06-18 |website=Alaska Public Media |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Ingvadóttir |first=Fanney Sigrún |date=2026-04-16 |title=Alaska Governor Mike Dunleavy appointed as USARC Commissioner |url=https://arcticportal.org/ap-library/news/https%3A%2F%2Farcticportal.org%2Fap-library%2Fnews%2F4082-alaska-governor-mike-dunleavy-appointed-as-usarc-commissioner |access-date=2026-06-18 |website=Arctic Portal - The Arctic Gateway |language=en}}</ref>
